<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project DefaultTargets="Build" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <!--
    lt: liblt, the engine, as a DLL (MIGRATION_NOTES.md §5.2). The sources are what the original's
    file(GLOB_RECURSE src/liblt/*.cpp) found, in the same order, except that XAudio2.cpp replaces
    Fmod.cpp and MusicEngine.cpp (ADR-003). A new .cpp now has to be added here and in the .filters;
    nothing globs it in any more. The headers are listed for the IDE only.

    92 of the sources share their file name with another one (six Custom.cpp, three Camera.cpp, ...).
    Each of those compiles into an object folder named after its source folder (ObjectFileName), as
    the original gave them explicit object names; in one folder their objects would overwrite each
    other. A new source whose name is already taken needs the same.

    Compile settings are the original's generated project's (§9.3):
    - /EHs rather than /EHsc: the original appends /EHs, which replaces the default /EHsc.
    - /fp:fast, /MP, and /arch:SSE2 on x64. There is no ARM64 counterpart: the original never
      targeted it, and an ARM64 /arch has no meaning here.
    - /NODEFAULTLIB:libcmt, as the original gives lt (and, through the EXECUTABLES bug, not launch).
    - Two definitions that the original's generator added are gone: nothing reads them (§10).

    The link line keeps the original's order, with ADR-002's substitutions:
    - glew32s is built in this solution, and NeuronClient replaces FreeType and SFML (ADR-010,
      ADR-012);
    - xaudio2.lib, from the Windows SDK, stands where FMOD Ex's two libraries stood (ADR-003);
    - the Windows import libraries are the original's default set, without odbc32/odbccp32, which
      MSBuild would otherwise add.
    The references build the libraries first. They do not link them (LinkLibraryDependencies=false),
    which keeps the order explicit, as the original did. NeuronClient's is the exception: its
    library is linked through its reference (ADR-005).

    The original's POST_BUILD step copied the FMOD Ex, FreeType and zlib DLLs next to lt.dll. None of
    them is left to copy: DirectWrite and XAudio2, which replace them, are part of Windows.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Label="ProjectConfigurations">
    <ProjectConfiguration Include="Debug|x64">
      <Configuration>Debug</Configuration>
      <Platform>x64</Platform>
    </ProjectConfiguration>
    <ProjectConfiguration Include="Release|x64">
      <Configuration>Release</Configuration>
      <Platform>x64</Platform>
    </ProjectConfiguration>
    <ProjectConfiguration Include="Debug|ARM64">
      <Configuration>Debug</Configuration>
      <Platform>ARM64</Platform>
    </ProjectConfiguration>
    <ProjectConfiguration Include="Release|ARM64">
      <Configuration>Release</Configuration>
      <Platform>ARM64</Platform>
    </ProjectConfiguration>
  </ItemGroup>
